this is code s3

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "PublicReadGetObject",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::your-bucket-name/*"
    }
  ]
}
##########################################################################################################
✅ Explanation of Each Line:

Part	                                   Meaning

Version                       	AWS policy version. Always use "2012-10-17" for modern policies.
Statement	                     The list of permissions you are granting.
Sid                           	Statement ID. Just a name: "PublicReadGetObject" (for your reference).
Effect                        	"Allow" → You are allowing access.
Principal                     	"*" → Means anyone in the world (public access).
Action                        	"s3:GetObject" → Allow action to download/view objects in S3.
Resource                      	"arn:aws:s3:::your-bucket-name/*" → Applies to all files in the bucket.

