{
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Id": "Policy1697075884818",
    "Statement": [
        {
            "Sid": "Stmt1697075871251",
            "Effect": "Deny",
            "Principal": {
                "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::000961310877:user/test"
            },
            "Action": [
                "s3:DeleteObject",
                "s3:DeleteObjectVersion",
                "s3:GetBucketPolicy",
                "s3:PutObject"
            ],
            "Resource": [
                "arn:aws:s3:::project-dsk-boss",
                "arn:aws:s3:::project-dsk-boss/*"
            ]
        }
    ]
}
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🧠 Explanation (Line by Line)
🔹 "Id": "Policy1697075884818"

Just a name/identifier for this policy

Used for reference only

🔹 "Version": "2012-10-17"

Policy language version

This is the latest and standard version AWS uses

🔹 "Statement"

A list of permission rules

Here, there is only one rule

🔹 "Sid": "Stmt1697075871251"

Statement ID

Helps identify this rule inside the policy

🔹 "Action"

These are the S3 operations being controlled:

Action	Meaning
s3:PutObject	Upload a file
s3:DeleteObject	Delete a file
s3:DeleteObjectVersion	Delete a versioned file
s3:GetBucketPolicy	View bucket policy
🔹 "Effect": "Deny"

This means block these actions

❗ Deny always overrides Allow in AWS

🔹 "Resource"

Defines where this deny applies:

arn:aws:s3:::yvt.avinash.telugu → the bucket itself

arn:aws:s3:::yvt.avinash.telugu/* → all objects inside the bucket

So this applies to bucket + all files.

🔹 "Principal"

Defines WHO this rule applies to:

IAM user: policytest

AWS Account: 501170964283

Only this user is affected by this policy.

🧪 Final Result (What the user can/cannot do)
Action	Result
Upload file	❌ Denied
Delete file	❌ Denied
Delete version	❌ Denied
View bucket policy	❌ Denied

Even if the user has admin access, this policy still blocks these actions.
